	"descriptionMarkdown": "# Mixed refuel station\n\nThe stations for 1 or 2 locomotives will provide your trains with the best 3 same stacks of quality rocket fuel or nuclear fuel available. It currently selects nuclear fuel over rocket fuel - and ascending quality. Any left-over fuel will be removed when the train enters the station.\n\nThe train station is setup to serve only if it has at least 3 full stacks of fuel - no mixes. If a station gets stuck - unable to serve for more than 5 minutes an alarm will be raised.\n\nVarious indicators try to indicate its current state - e.g. unloading, loading, which fuel has at least 3 stacks and which fuel it determines the best.\n\nIt requires the [mod Inventory sensor](https://mods.factorio.com/mod/Inventory%20Sensor) to function - as individual rocket fuel cannot be detected within vanilla game boundaries.\n\nAdvantages:\n\n*  easy refueling of trains \n* lots of status effects\n\ndisadvantages:\n* requires a mod\n* refueling condition is limited to <=1 - as rocket fuel and nuclear fuel have so different stack sizes. Meaning there is a risk that your train might run out of fuel to the station with rocket fuel.  You can increase the limit to 10 if you do not use nuclear fuel.",
